    <h1>“COFFEE DOESN’T PRODUCE CANCER” says leading American Scientist</h1>
    <p class="muted">By John Goerke. <time datetime="2018-02-13">February 13, 2018</time> (updated <time datetime="2018-11-16">November 16, 2018</time>).</p>

    <p>This is a historical article, kept as originally framed in 2018. It is general information, not medical advice, and Bona Fide does not add to or endorse the claims it discusses; talk to a health professional about your own situation.</p>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>The article discusses California's Proposition 65 and acrylamide in the context of coffee, and refers to an editorial by Edward L. Giovannucci on the subject. It is summarised here rather than reproduced.</p>
    <p>Searches such as “organic coffee for cancer” reach this historical article; Bona Fide makes no health claim about organic coffee here, and nothing on this page is medical advice.</p>

    <p>Read more in <a href="/is-coffee-healthy/">Is Coffee Healthy</a> or return to the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>.</p>
